<title>UK: UK card spending up yr/yr 4.3 pct in Feb - CCRG.</title>
<headline>UK card spending up yr/yr 4.3 pct in Feb - CCRG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Credit Card Research Group, representing major UK credit and debit card issuers, released the following consumer spending figures for February 1997 -</p>
<p> CARD EXPENDITURE (in million stg) *   Feb	 Jan     % change</p>
<p> All sectors - total		   7,216     6,919    4.3</p>
<p> Food and drink			  1,883     1,737    8.4</p>
<p> Mixed business			    530	 558   -5.1</p>
<p> Clothing				    381	 422   -9.6</p>
<p> Household				   657	 687   -4.4</p>
<p> Motoring				  1,019	 940    8.4</p>
<p> Entertainment			     400	 361   10.8</p>
<p> Hotels					229	 188   21.4</p>
<p> Travel					712	 729   -2.3</p>
<p> Services				    593	 549    8.1</p>
<p>Credit Card Research Group director Elizabeth Philips said the return to growth in card spending shows that most cardholders have paid off their Christmas bills by mid-February and are ready to use their cards again.</p>
<p>NOTE * figures adjusted for variations in the number of processing days between months.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
